  "Question": "The average age of \\(5\\) people in a room is \\(30\\) years. An \\(18\\)-year-old person leaves the room. What is the average age of the four remaining people?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(25\\)",
    "B": "\\(26\\)",
    "C": "\\(29\\)",
    "D": "\\(33\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The original average lets us find the total age before removing the person who leaves. The five people's ages sum to \\(5\\cdot30=150\\) years. Removing the \\(18\\)-year-old leaves \\(150-18=132\\) years among four people. Their average age is therefore\n\\[\n132\\div4=33\n\\]\nyears, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
